# Game_BeepTest — Beep Test / Luc Leger (ID 12)
# Files: src/coordinator/Game_BeepTest.h, Game_BeepTest.cpp
# HTML: data/game_beep_setup.html, game_beep_names.html, game_beep_run.html

## GAMEPLAY
Progressive shuttle run fitness test. Players alternate between 2 pucks following accelerating beep schedule.
21 levels with increasing laps and speed. 2 yellow cards = elimination. VO2max estimated.

## CONFIG
- numPlayers (1-10), 2 pucks per player (start + target)

## STATES
BEEP_SETUP → BEEP_WAIT_HANDS → BEEP_COUNTDOWN (3s, SKI) → BEEP_RUNNING → BEEP_FINISHED
Optional: BEEP_FALSE_START (2s penalty)

## KEY MECHANICS
- Schedule pre-calculation: 200 lap timestamps based on progressive speeds
- Speed: 8.5 + (level * 0.5) km/h, levels 1-21
- lapsPerLevel[21]: 7 to 15 laps per level
- Duration per lap: 72000ms / speed
- Player visual states: 0=chase, 1=yellow warning, 2=hit window, 3=waiting
- 2s timeout past beep → auto yellow card + advance
- Press >1.5s before beep → yellow card
- 2 yellow cards → elimination + explosion sound
- VO2max = (speed * 6.55) - 35.8

## COMMANDS
setup, cfg_players, start, reset, stop, exit, elim_player, clear_card

## STATUS JSON
{st, tT (test time), spd, lvl, players: [{id, elim, hld, fs, yc (yellow cards), dist (lap*20), vo2}]}
